7. Source code of GPL and LGPL components

Our images, horus-mas, horus-agent, horus-knowledge-store and horus-web-client,
contain operating-system packages from Debian and Alpine Linux licensed under
the GNU GPL or the GNU LGPL (7.1 and 7.2). They run as separate programs, or
are system libraries that the Python and Node.js runtimes load; Horus's own
code does not link them. Two libraries among our dependencies are under the
LGPL too (7.3): psycopg2-binary, and the prebuilt libvips that sharp loads.

Where the source is:

- Debian packages: the source package of each version listed below (.dsc,
  original and Debian tarballs) is on https://snapshot.debian.org/, which keeps
  every version Debian has published.
- Alpine packages: the build recipe and patches at the aports commit listed for
  each package, in https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports, and the
  upstream archives it names, mirrored at
  https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/.
- psycopg2-binary: its source distribution on PyPI; sharp's libvips: its
  package on npm. 7.3 gives the links.

